# DDD Layers

## Domain — pure TypeScript only

| Folder | Rules |
|--------|--------|
| `aggregates/` | `AggregateRoot<T>`, static `create`, private `#` fields, events on mutations |
| `entities/` | `BaseDomain<T>`, live inside aggregate, **no repository** |
| `value-objects/` | Immutable, no `id`, structural `equals()`, static factory |
| `events/` | Past tense, extend `DomainEvent`, one per domain method |
| `errors/` | Extend `BusinessError` + `errorCode`; no raw `Error` / `HttpException` |
| `services/` | Pure class, no `@Injectable`, no repo calls |
| `repositories/` | Interface + `Symbol` token = name; **roots only**; extends `IRepository` |
| `ports/` | External contracts only; token = interface name |
| `policies/` | Pure `isSatisfiedBy` / question methods; no I/O |
| `enums/` | String enums only |

`CorrespondenceRequestEvent` is application-layer only — never emit from domain models.

## Application — orchestration only

- Commands: load → domain method → `repo.save` → `eventBus.publishAll` → `clearEvents`
- Queries: read-only, return **DTO** (never raw aggregate)
- Event handlers: one side effect; mutate via new command, not in-handler
- Inject same-module repo/ports by token; other modules via Facade / read ports
- DTOs in `dtos/`; mappers are static domain → response DTO
- `ICurrentUserPort` for role/permission checks; pass `userId` in command when it is business intent

## Presentation — HTTP boundary

- Controllers inject **only** `CommandBus` / `QueryBus` — never repos, handlers, or domain
- Explicit `Promise<T>` return type + `@ApiAutoResponse*` on every method
- Never construct `SuccessResponse` — global interceptor wraps
- Auth/RBAC from `@lib/auth`; permissions = `action:resource` (e.g. `read:roles`)
- Feature guards only for ownership etc.; never reimplement JWT/RBAC

## Infrastructure — implements ports

- Prisma repos extend `PrismaCrudRepositoryBase`; implement all five hooks:
  `toDomain`, `toCreateInput`, `toUpdateInput`, `toUniqueWhere`, `toFilterWhere`
- Override `supportsSoftDelete()` / `defaultOrderBy()` when needed
- Adapters map transport errors → `BusinessError` before throwing
- **No N+1** — batch with `findByIds` / `{ id: { in: ids } }`; early-exit on empty
- Cache behind repo/adapter only; namespaced keys + TTL; invalidate on write
